From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:33:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] feat(sim_display): SIM_DISPLAY_OUTPUT=sbs_full, full side
 by side for a stereo compositor

A seventh rendering mode, "Full SBS": two views, each rendered at the window's
full resolution (view scale 1.0 x 1.0, 2x1 tiles, Kooima over the whole
display like Anaglyph), handed over side by side, left first, as they are.
The existing "sbs" crops the centre of each view and scales it, and
"squeezed" halves each view's width, so neither can be shown per eye at the
resolution it was rendered at.

The VK DP reports XRT_DP_SCANOUT_FLAG_FULL_SIDE_BY_SIDE for this mode and
draws it with the squeezed-SBS kernel (each tile into its half of the
target): with the target twice the window's width, which the runtime
presents when it can declare the window, that is a 1:1 copy of each view.
Every DP variant maps the mode to that pipeline through one shared helper
before indexing its table; the D3D11, D3D12 and Metal logs say the output is
flat there, since no declaration exists on those backends.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>

Origin: vendor, https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/commit/91454d96a8066d4b04644c8037cc75fb00008c01
Forwarded: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/displayxr-runtime/tree/order34-sbs-declare (the pull request to DisplayXR follows the answer on https://github.com/DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime/issues/1928)
Comment: Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 34; made on v2.65.0, applied to v2.66.3 without conflict.
